@title Data subject access requests
@subtitle Quillfeather Software privacy runbook
@author Privacy Officer

kpi Response due | 30 days | +60 days for complex requests only | neutral
kpi Internal target | day 25 | deliver the export | good
kpi Identity check | 5 business days | two documents | neutral

# Deadlines
We must respond within 30 days of receiving a valid request. For complex requests only, we can extend this by up to 60 more days, but only if we tell the requester within the first 30 days. Our internal target is to deliver by day 25.

# Handling steps
1. Log the request in the privacy tracker within 1 business day.
2. Verify identity within 5 business days.
-- a) Ask for two documents.
-- b) Never accept a photo of a card that shows a full number.
3. Confirm the scope with the requester by email.
4. Collect data from the six systems listed below.
5. Legal reviews the export and redacts other people's data.
6. Package the export.
-- a) Use an encrypted ZIP.
-- b) Send the password by SMS, never in the same email.
7. Deliver by day 25 and record the delivery date.
8. Close the ticket and keep the log for 3 years.

# Systems to search
table = System,Owner,Days needed; CRM,Sales Ops,3; Billing,Finance Systems,4; Support desk,Support Ops,3; Product database,Data Platform,6; Marketing email,Growth,2; Analytics events,Data Platform,6

Backups are not searched, but note the date of the last backup.

# Do not
- Do not delete data in response to an access request.
- Do not send the export to an address that was not verified.
- Do not discuss the request in public channels.

